    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the advice. i'm seeing some pretty strong correlations in the preliminary data where high-growth areas for certain minority groups are also seeing the highest jumps in larceny. i want to make sure my model isn't just picking up noise. given the specific nature of these trends, would it be more accurate to treat ethnicity as a primary driver in the risk coefficient, or should i be looking at other socioeconomic indicators first? i just want to be sure i'm capturing the actual risk factors correctly for our underwriting guidelines.",
